<content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>A marine biologist estimates that a structure of coral has a volume of 1,200 cubic centimeters and that its volume
  doubles each year.</para>
<para><image height="300" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/915e980323c039f033c1086572a5d1f032cef8c3" width="300"/></para>
<br/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
      <item>Write an equation of the form \(y=a\cdot b^t\) representing the relationship, where \(t\) is time in
        years since the coral was measured and \(y\) is volume of coral in cubic centimeters. (You need to figure
        out what numbers \(a\) and \(b\) are in this situation.)</item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
    </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(y=1,200\cdot 2^t\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><br/>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the volume of the coral when \(t\) is 5, 1, 0, –1, and –2. Note that when \(t = -1\), this
    represents one year before the marine biologist made the original estimate.<br/>
  </item>
</list>
